    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) by putting each piece in its natural place:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter, alongside the other owner attributes.\n\n2. **`CustomerCodeGenerator`** (new, `service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java`) \u2014 a small `@Component` with a single responsibility: formatting the code. It upper-cases the first three letters of the last name and zero-pads the sequence to four digits (`String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`). It takes the sequence as a parameter so it stays free of persistence concerns.\n\n3. **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 the service already owns the `OwnerRepository`, so it computes the global sequence (`findAll().size() + 1`) and delegates formatting to the generator, assigning the code only for new owners that don't already have one. Update paths (existing owners) are untouched.\n\n4. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps `Owner.customerCode \u2192 OwnerDto.customerCode` automatically (same mechanism as `displayName`/`initials`). No mapper code changes were needed.\n\n5. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four `owners` tables (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql). The test profile is hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is what actually makes the column exist for the tests.\n\nThe `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The two created owners get `SMI-####` / `JON-####` with consecutive sequence numbers, driven by the global owner count.\n\nI left the legacy JDBC repository impl (a non-default, untested profile) untouched, since it already omits newer fields like `email` and `registrationDate` \u2014 adding only `customer_code` there would be inconsistent with its existing scope.",
